{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 123, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "With edge 4 absent the output node has fewer incoming paths, so adding a conv path on edge 3 adds more capacity and connectivity."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "When the direct input-to-output edge is missing, a conv on edge 4 supplies a critical path to the output."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing edge 4 when edge 3 is already absent can sever or starve the output node, causing large accuracy drops."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "A conv on edge 4 provides a redundant route to the output, cushioning the loss of edge 3."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a conv into the output via node 2 matters more when the node-1-to-output path is missing."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing edge 1's op with pooling is far less harmful when another conv exists on edge 0, whereas it is catastrophic if edge 1 held the only conv."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "Cells built from parameter-free ops gain enormously from their first convolution, while conv-rich cells are near saturation."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "A conv on edge 2 adds much-needed learnable capacity when the upstream edge is a parameter-free skip."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lo